there's so many. I give some of the same notes so&nbsp;
much that I have I now have a template of notes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.760
right so that you know back in the day I used to&nbsp;
have to rewrite the same note over and over and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:24.240
over but now I kind of have a template of some of&nbsp;
the notices I give the most often but I think the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:31.620
largest one is lack of a goal or a problem to&nbsp;
solve and lack of an inciting incident because&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.620 --> 00:00:37.500
the inciting incident causes the goal or the&nbsp;
problem to solve so usually if there is no goal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:42.600
or no problem it's because there was nothing that&nbsp;
caused it and so I end up giving those two things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:48.480
or I'll say your inciting incident is very clear&nbsp;
this is what it is and anytime I do it I follow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:53.340
it up with this is what it is that way the writer&nbsp;
can go that's not what it is and they can realize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:58.380
oh well it's not as clear as you thought it was&nbsp;
right but just because you have a clear inciting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:04.860
incident doesn't mean you now have a clear goal or&nbsp;
a clear problem and so that's the nuts and bolts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:11.580
of what your screenplay is so if your inciting&nbsp;
incident isn't clear and if the goal that they're&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.580 --> 00:01:16.500
